			"interpretation": "Scope owns the common module's platform-service layer: AccountService (lazy singleton over AccountKit HuaweiID auth), PushServiceManager plus PushService (notification-enable and push-token upload), UpdateService (AppGallery update check/dialog), and ~35 static utility adapters under util re-exported through the index.ets barrel. Observable behavior: serviceInit() subscribes to distributed-account login/logout common events, restores the persisted UserAccount from PreferenceManager key 'userAccount', queries HuaweiIDProvider state and resolves InitResult{isLogin,needUpdate}; login() runs a forced authorization (profile scope, serviceauthcode, PS256, random state checked against response state); logout paths clear nickname/unionId/avatarUrl, persist 'userLogin', and emit BIND_LOGOUT_EVENT. PushServiceManager requests notification enable then posts pushService.getToken() to PushService, a stub resolving true. UpdateService guards canIUse, derives UIAbilityContext from AppStorage UI_CONTEXT, and rejects BusinessError-like objects when context or capability is missing. Public boundary: singleton classes and stateless static utils exposing Promise<boolean>, InitResult, PushTokenParams; cross-boundary relations import out-of-scope storagemanager/PreferenceManager and constant/CommonConstants event ids. Maintenance contract: preserve singleton semantics, emitted events, preference keys, TAG-prefixed hilog logging (domain 0xFF00, prefix '[HMOSWorld]'), login state validation, and the index.ets barrel; PushService.postPushToken is an intentional integration seam.",
